    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 the single acceptance test (`coreDerivesAgeBand`) passes, confirming the full chain works end-to-end.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner age-band derivation. The request may now include `birthDate` (ISO), and the response returns `ageBand` computed as of the registration date.\n\n**Design** \u2014 each piece of logic lives in its own small unit, reusing existing patterns:\n\n1. **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 an enum `MINOR/ADULT/SENIOR` with a single static `asOf(birthDate, referenceDate)` factory holding the banding rule (<18 \u2192 MINOR, 18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT, \u226565 \u2192 SENIOR, null when a date is missing). This keeps the calendar arithmetic in one testable place rather than inlined in the entity.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, plus a transient `getAgeBand()` derived getter that delegates to `AgeBand.asOf(birthDate, registrationDate)`. It returns a `String` (or null), mirroring the existing `getContactPreference()` derived-enum getter so MapStruct maps it to the DTO enum automatically \u2014 no mapper changes needed.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (input, `format: date`) to `OwnerFields`, and `ageBand` (read-only enum) to `Owner`, so the generated DTOs carry both fields and MapStruct wires them by name.\n\n4. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column so Hibernate (the active `spring-data-jpa` profile) can persist and re-read it.\n\nThe controller and mapper required no edits \u2014 `birthDate` flows in via the existing `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` mapping, and `ageBand` flows out via the existing name-based `toOwnerDto` mapping, evaluated against the already-adjusted registration date. I left the JDBC repository untouched since it maps none of the recent owner columns (it's out of the active test profile and out of scope).",
